In Java 25, `I` is a `sealed` interface permitting `A`, `B` and `record C(int j)`, and `record IPair(I i, I j)` is switched over with the labels shown. Which value matches none of them?

```java
switch (p) {
    case IPair(A a1, A a2) -> 0;
    case IPair(B b1, B b2) -> 1;
    case IPair(C c1, C c2) -> 2;
}
```
